6066 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/P 4816 0 R/S/Figure/Alt(A golden balance scale with blue and red weights stands beside a large book, symbolizing the positive and negative felt experiences considered across a conscious life. The illustration introduces the Law of Fairness as a new way of looking beyond outward circumstances to the experience of life from within.\nPrinted panel text:\nTHE LAW OF FAIRNESS. A new way of seeing every life.\nWe judge fairness by the visible shape of a life: health and hardship, love and loss, opportunity and misfortune. Yet life is not lived from the outside. It is lived within consciousness, through joy and sorrow, pleasure and pain, peace and fear.\nCould life be fair where it is actually lived, even when it appears profoundly unfair from the outside? The Law of Fairness proposes that every felt experience carries weight according to its intensity and duration. Across the completed conscious life, total positive and negative feeling exactly balance.\nPicture a scale open for a lifetime. Joy and relief add weight to one side; pain and grief to the other. It may tip heavily for years, but when the conscious life is complete, the two sides balance. Each life carries its own scale. No life balances another.\nLives may differ enormously in length, choices, pleasures, wounds, and circumstances. The scale weighs neither wealth nor virtue, status nor faith. It weighs felt experience alone. Circumstances tell the visible story of a life, but feeling is how that story is lived. The Law asks us not to mistake the visible story for the whole.)/K[0]/Pg 47 0 R/A 6068 0 R>>
endobj

