6084 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/P 4816 0 R/S/Figure/Alt(An open book beneath a growing tree is surrounded by scenes of people researching, cooperating, and connecting with one another. The illustration represents the shared work of reading and discussing the ideas, testing the Law through serious inquiry, strengthening what can be learned, and using that knowledge to help reduce suffering and build a more peaceful world.\nPrinted panel text:\nTHE WORK AHEAD. A shared mission to build a better world.\nRead the books, share them, and bring the Law of Fairness into classrooms, research groups, reading circles, and community conversations. Important ideas grow stronger when people examine them together, challenge assumptions, compare perspectives, and turn understanding into shared effort.\nScientists, researchers, clinicians, philosophers, and other experts can help test the Law, refine its measurements, improve its methods, and compare it with strong rivals. Serious criticism is essential. It exposes weaknesses, sharpens the questions, and helps reveal what should endure, what needs revision, and what should be rejected.\nBeyond the hypothesis lies a practical challenge: building a world with less corruption and needless suffering, and more room for dignity, freedom, meaning, beauty, and opportunity. If this project speaks to you, bring your knowledge, experience, curiosity, and determination. Progress begins when people from different paths meet, share what they know, and build what survives scrutiny.\nHelp us make this generation the one that brought peace to our world.)/K[0]/Pg 50 0 R/A 6086 0 R>>
endobj

